Plan risks:
- R1: Simulation runtime — 20 seeds × 2 scenarios × (1h+4h+8h); event-driven loop, cycle count ~45k — fast. However, if Phase B mistakenly implements a 1-second-tick loop, 28800 ticks × 20 × 2 × ... ≈ 28800+14400+3600=... total virtual seconds per seed-scenario = 13 hours = 46800 seconds → 1-second-tick loop = 46800 iterations per seed-scenario × 40 = 1.9 million tick_effective calls — still no problem in GDScript (<10 seconds). OK, no runtime risk; however, each tick allocates an Array — no problem.
- R2: Determinism of float accumulation — tick step 1.0 sec fixed; _stage_elapsed uses float accumulation; determinism holds within the same execution order; the determinism check runs the same sequence twice and compares digests computed from integer/string event fields (event IDs, species, rounded seconds) — avoid digesting raw floats.
- R3: UTC timestamps — commit_catch requires a valid UTC string; derive it deterministically from a virtual clock with pure integer civil-time conversion anchored to a fixed epoch 2026-01-01T00:00:00Z; do not use Time.get_datetime_string... Actually Godot's Time.get_datetime_string_from_unix_seconds is deterministic; however, to keep the digest fully independent of the engine, a pure-int helper within the sim is preferable. Plan: use `Time.get_datetime_string_from_unix_seconds(epoch0 + int(clock.now()), true)` — Godot 4.x has this static; it returns "YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SS" without a Z? There's a use_utc argument. Hmm, risk of format mismatch (no trailing Z). Safer: implement a pure-int civil-time formatter in the sim script. Note both options, with the requirement: output must match FishInstance.UTC_PATTERN and be deterministic across machines.
- R4: sale_id and catch_id are unique — derive from RNG events (the FSM already provides unique catch IDs via RNG; sale IDs from a per-seed counter).
- R5: No writing to res:// from the sim — sim only outputs to stdout; the runner writes evidence files into the real ROOT's tasks/evidence/SIM-001/. The Godot steps run only inside a temporary isolated copy (convention: no Godot launch against a real project path). The sim writes no files (memory-only scenarios), the fault-injection scenario writes to a temp save dir via configure_dir (absolute path under a temp directory), and never writes to user:// (isolated HOME would also work — but configure_dir to an absolute temp directory is cleaner; save_service's DEFAULT_DIR is user://; the save test in SAVE-001 probably used configure_dir with an isolated HOME. Use configure_dir(temp_save_dir)).
- R6: Full 20-seed run — runtime is bounded by the runner's per-step TIMEOUT (600s per step, same as the save runner).
- R7: Report must not self-adjust numbers: preflight numeric lock (R-4 style), fail if data/*.json is out of sync; the sim only reads configs via the FishSpeciesCatalog/RuntimeConfig loaders.

